    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "28d874f2_0ff32152",
        "filename": "media/ndk/NdkMediaCodecStore.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 36
      },
      "lineNbr": 88,
      "author": {
        "id": 1021605
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-19T18:02:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "we don\u0027t actually need a linked list, but it will make iterating through the infos much easier. Unfortunately C++ doesn\u0027t provide a quick container for that, but you can piece one together.\n\nWe do need a name \u003d\u003e info map\n\nWe also need a media_type \u003d\u003e std::list map\n\nYou will need to then iterate through sCodecList (this is strongly ordered by convention), and for each codec, iterate through the supported types (these are arbitrarily ordered, but since we maintain an ordered list for each media type, it does not matter.)\n\nIf there is a single supported media type, the NDK name of the codec will be the same as the SDK name, simply create an AMediaCodecInfo with the sole supported type, and add it to the map using the codec name, and also to the end of the list for the media type.\n\nIf there are multiple supported media types, we need to disambiguate the names. We could add the type to the end of the name (after the /), e.g.\n\nc2.vendor.vpx.decoder for video/x.on2.vp8 would become c2.vendor.vpx.decoder.x.on2.vp8, and if such a name is already registered (unlikely), we could add a \".1\", \".2\" at the end. (Coding it is a bit tedious, sorry.)\n\nIn the unlikely event that a single-type-codec conflicts with a generated disambiguiated name, we will need to add \".1\", \".2\" to that as well. (This is extremely unlikely, but we need to handle it.)\n\npseudo code:\n\n```\n\n  for (sCodecInfo : sCodecInfos) {\n    bool useTypeSuffix \u003d sCodecInfo-\u003egetSupportedTypes().size() \u003e 1;\n    for (sType : sCodecInfo-\u003egetSupportedTypes()) {\n      size_t slashIx \u003d sType.find_last_of(\u0027/\u0027);\n      if (slashIx \u003d\u003d std::string::npos) {\n        slashIx \u003d 0;\n      } else {\n        slashIx ++;\n      }\n      int copyIx \u003d 0;\n      std::string ndkBaseName \u003d sCodecInfo-\u003egetName();\n      if (useTypeSuffix) {\n          ndkBaseName +\u003d \".\" + sType.substr(slashIx);\n      }\n      std::string ndkName;\n      while (true) {\n        ndkName \u003d ndkBaseName;\n        if (copyIx) {\n          ndkName +\u003d \".\" + std::tostring(copyIx);\n        }\n        if (!nameToInfoMap.contains(ndkName)) {\n          break;\n        }\n        copyIx +\u003d 1;\n      }\n     \n     create AMediaCodecInfo with the ndkName and the codec type.    \n     insert it into nameToInfoMap, and typeToInfoList.\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 71,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 88,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "d507eb112c74344f9a2238145fdf2942a2d6e5d1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
